e and in animal models</article-title><source><italic>Antimicrobial Agents and Chemotherapy</italic></source><year>1998</year><volume>42</volume><issue>8</issue><fpage>1959</fpage><lpage>1965</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9687390</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B35"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zardi</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Picardi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Afeltra</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Treatment of cryptosporidiosis in immunocompromised hosts: still an open question</article-title><source><italic>Chemotherapy</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>51</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>193</fpage><lpage>196</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16006765</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gargala</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Drug treatment and novel drug target against Cryptosporidium</article-title><source><italic>Parasite</italic></source><year>2008</year><volume>15</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>275</fpage><lpage>281</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18814694</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B34"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DNA topoisomerases</article-title><source><italic>Annual Review of Biochemistry</italic></source><year>1996</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>635</fpage><lpage>692</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B6"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Champoux</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DNA topoisomerases: structure, function, and mechanism</article-title><source><italic>Annual Review of Biochemistry</italic></source><year>2001</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>369</fpage><lpage>413</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Corbett</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></name><name><surname>Berger</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structure, molecular mechanisms, and evolutionary relationships in DNA topoisomerases</article-title><source><italic>Annual Review of Biophysics and Biomolecular Structure</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>95</fpage><lpage>118</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>16</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mdluli</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ma</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mycobacterium tuberculosis DNA gyrase as a target for drug discovery</article-title><source><italic>Infectious Disorders: Drug Targets</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>7</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>159</fpage><lpage>168</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17970226</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>17</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cheesman</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The topoisomerases of protozoan parasites</article-title><source><italic>Parasitology Today</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>16</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>281</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10858645</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B2"><label>18</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bakshi</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name><name><surname>Shapiro</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DNA topoisomerases as targets for antiprotozoal therapy</article-title><source><italic>Mini Reviews in Medicinal Chemistry</italic></source><year>2003</year><volume>3</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>597</fpage><lpage>608</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12871162</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B3"><label>19</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bala&#x000f1;a-Fouce</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Redondo</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>P&#x000e9;rez-Pertejo</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>D&#x000ed;az-Gonz&#x000e1;lez</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Reguera</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Targeting atypical trypanosomatid DNA topoisomerase I</article-title><source><italic>Drug Discovery Today</italic></source><year>2006</year><volume>11</volume><issue>15-16</issue><fpage>733</fpage><lpage>740</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16846801</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B28"><label>20</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tosh</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kilbey</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The gene encoding topoisomerase I from the human malaria parasite Plasmodium falciparum</article-title><source><italic>Gene</italic></source><year>1995</year><volume>163</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>151</fpage><lpage>154</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7557466</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B29"><label>21</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tosh</surname><